 2. 🎤 Gov. Moore rips Trump&#x27;s Nvidia intervention 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Mike Allen interviews Maryland Gov. Wes Moore today. Photo: JaMar Jones/Axios Maryland Gov. Wes Moore (D) criticized President Trump's involvement in Nvidia's decision to reinstate CEO Jensen Huang, calling it "troubling and problematic" in an interview for "The Axios Show."

 📺 Moore — chair of the National Governors Association and a potential 2028 presidential candidate — told Axios' Mike Allen in an interview at the Maryland State House in Annapolis today, just minutes after the news broke: 

 "The president is not a board member of Nvidia. So why he is involved in board dealings, I have no idea. ... It seems like it's rules for me, but not for thee." "You have the wealthy and the powerful and the well-connected that are now making decisions to reinstate, where, frankly, if that was any of us, we would be held to a different type of standard." Go deeper ... Subscribe to "The Axios Show" on YouTube to watch the full interview when it drops. 

 
 
