 4. 🦃 1 for the road: Don&#x27;t forget to thaw 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios Thanksgiving is just a few days away — so don't forget to start thawing your turkey, if you bought a frozen bird.

 The USDA recommends 24 hours of fridge thawing for every 4–5 pounds of turkey. 🍗 Another tip: "Keep the turkey in its original packaging and place it on a tray or in a container to catch any juices."

 Cold-water thawing is a faster option — but you should cook your turkey right when it's ready to go. Go deeper . 

 
 
